---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: timeline-data-governance
purpose: "Timeline data (backlog, chronicle, roadmap). Every new entry carries id + kind so it is citable and schema-typed (see CONVENTIONS.md)."
rules:
  - id: timeline-entry-frontmatter
    class: ask
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    require-frontmatter: [id, kind]
    why: "New timeline entries need `id` (citation slug) and `kind` (schema type). See genesis/data/timeline/CONVENTIONS.md."
---
# timeline data — backlog / chronicle / roadmap

Every new entry under this tree (backlog, chronicle, roadmap) is born with `id` (citation slug) and
`kind` (schema type) per `CONVENTIONS.md`. The rule fires at birth on a schema-less entry and stays
silent on edits to the already-grandfathered entries. `roadmap/`, already conformant, sees no friction.
